prompt:
important historical Jewish events that happened in the USA, dates to the left of them
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
| Date          | Historical Jewish Event in the United States                                                                                                      |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **1654**      | First group of Jewish refugees arrives in New York City (then New Amsterdam), establishing the first permanent Jewish community in North America. |
| **1730**      | Dedication of Congregation Shearith Israel, the oldest Jewish congregation in the U.S.                                                            |
| **1790**      | George Washington writes his famous letter to the Hebrew Congregation of Newport affirming religious freedom for Jews.                            |
| **1843**      | Founding of B'nai B'rith in New York.                                                                                                             |
| **1881–1924** | Mass immigration of Eastern European Jews; over 2 million Jews arrive in the United States.                                                       |
| **1913**      | Creation of the Anti-Defamation League to combat antisemitism and discrimination.                                                                 |
| **1915**      | Lynching of Leo Frank in Georgia, a pivotal event in American Jewish history.                                                                     |
| **1939**      | The ship MS St. Louis carrying Jewish refugees is denied entry to the U.S. and forced to return to Europe.                                        |
| **1945**      | End of World War II; American Jewish organizations become heavily involved in aiding Holocaust survivors.                                         |
| **1948**      | President Harry S. Truman recognizes the State of Israel minutes after its declaration of independence.                                           |
| **1958**      | Dedication of the Touro Synagogue National Historic Site as a symbol of early American Jewish history.                                            |
| **1964–1965** | Many American Jews play prominent roles in the Civil Rights Movement and voting-rights campaigns.                                                 |
| **1978**      | Neo-Nazi attempt to march in Skokie sparks a major national debate over free speech and antisemitism.                                             |
| **1993**      | Opening of the United States Holocaust Memorial Museum.                                                                                           |
| **2018**      | Deadly attack on Tree of Life Synagogue, the deadliest antisemitic attack in U.S. history.                                                        |
